<!--
  Descriptor of the jetbrains.mps.ide.customization content module declared by MPSPlugin.template.xml.

  MPS-40020: ExternalProductResourceUrls decides where Help | Help, Help | What's New, the feedback forms and the
  patch/download URLs point. The platform declares a neutral implementation in the main descriptor
  (PlatformExtensions.xml, LegacyExternalProductResourceUrls), but MPS's product content also pulls in
  intellij.idea.customization.base (MPSProperties.getProductContentDescriptor), which overrides it with
  IntelliJIdeaExternalResourceUrls. That is a content module, and content modules are registered after the main
  descriptor, so MPS's own override in MPSPlugin.template.xml was silently beaten by IntelliJ IDEA's and MPS shipped
  IDEA's help and What's New pages. Registering the override here, from a descriptor that depends on
  intellij.idea.customization.base, is what puts it after IDEA's.

  The package prefix intentionally owns no code. A content module with no jar of its own is required to declare one
  (ClassLoaderConfigurator.getPackagePrefixesLoadedBySeparateClassLoaders), but claiming the package that actually
  holds MPSExternalResourceUrls would take it away from the core class loader, and MPSPlugin.template.xml has to keep
  registering the same implementation - see the comment there. A prefix that matches nothing satisfies the
  requirement while leaving the class on the core loader: this module's loader finds no match for the class name,
  createModuleResolveScopeManager returns "" ("not mine"), and PluginClassLoader delegates to the core loader.
  Do not move code into jetbrains.mps.ide.customization - keep the prefix empty.

  Known wart: IDEA's registration is not declared open="true", so overriding it logs
  "InstanceNotOverridableException: Incorrect override for ...ExternalProductResourceUrls" at WARN. The override is
  applied regardless. MPS already carries a few of these (FileDocumentManager, AbstractVcsHelper). Note that
  InstanceContainerImpl tolerates incorrect overrides only by default and its comment says the default "will be
  changed to false" once the platform migration finishes - at which point these become LOG.error, i.e. auto-reported
  exceptions. The clean way out for this one is to stop pulling intellij.idea.customization.base into MPS's product
  content (MPSProperties.getProductContentDescriptor) - it holds nothing but IDEA branding, two services - and then
  the registration in MPSPlugin.template.xml alone is correct and this module can go away.
-->
<idea-plugin package="jetbrains.mps.ide.customization">
  <dependencies>
    <module name="intellij.idea.customization.base"/>
  </dependencies>
  <extensions defaultExtensionNs="com.intellij">
    <applicationService serviceInterface="com.intellij.platform.ide.customization.ExternalProductResourceUrls"
                        serviceImplementation="jetbrains.mps.intellij.integration.MPSExternalResourceUrls"
                        overrides="true"/>
  </extensions>
</idea-plugin>
